We created a plugin for NMRFx using IntelliJ IDEA via the following:


1. Imported the Plugin Module into IntelliJ

• Open the NMRFx project in IntelliJ.
• File -> Project Structure -> Modules.
• Import Module - point to plugin project's pom.xml

2. Added plugin as dependency in main project's pom.xml

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>edu.umbc.hhmi</groupId>
            <artifactId>umbc_nmrfx_plugin</artifactId>
            <version>12.0.9-1</version>
            <scope>runtime</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    2. EDIT. We will take a different tack to avoid meddling with NMRFx source code. We have set up a run configuration
    in IntelliJ and added the plugin path to the classpath. Need to remember to recompile the plugin before debugging.


3. Registered the Plugin for ServiceLoader Discovery

• Inside the plugin's src/main/resources/ directory, create META-INF/services/.
• Created a plain text file named after the fully qualified name of the Plugin Interface
• Inside this file, added a single line containing the fully qualified name of the plugin
